<title>CROATIA: Croatia guarantees loan to bail Rijeka port.</title>
<headline>Croatia guarantees loan to bail Rijeka port.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Croatian government will guarantee a 15 million German mark loan from Austria's Raiffeisenbank to bail Rijeka port out of old debts, according to financial weekly Privredni Vjesnik.</p>
<p>It said the loan was repayable over four years at 8.85 percent annual interest. It would replace the port company's old short-term liabilities to help it consolidate its position.</p>
<p>The newspaper did not give any figures for its total outstanding debt. The government has passed a restructuring programme for the troubled port, which handles most of Croatia's naval imports and exports. -- Kolumbina Bencevic, Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
